---
/* The four capability slots. Order is fixed: index 0 is the selected service after a pick,
   indices 1-3 become that service's subcategories. All sizing is computed in fitSlots().

   Mobile: inside a service section the four stacked slots collapse to a single-line auto-
   scrolling marquee ([data-sub-marquee]) so the chrome eats far less height and the galleries
   get more of the frame. The controller adds data-mq to [data-bar] and fills the marquee; the
   real slots (which carry the scramble, hover, click-nav and the field-luminance pools) are
   hidden then — the field is dissolved in a section, so nothing depends on their positions. On
   the hero and on desktop the slots render as before.

   --cap-sep is the one knob for the labels' separation from the ASCII field
   behind them. It is the whole `filter` value: three stacked drop-shadows, a
   tight one that reads as an edge and two very wide ones that read as nothing
   in particular — just the field sitting a layer further back under each word.
   All in em, so the halo scales with the fitted label size; on a phone the
   stacked names' halos run into one another and become one band, which is the
   intent. Tune it here.

   drop-shadow, NOT text-shadow. In the hero these labels are painted as a
   gradient clipped to the glyphs with a transparent text fill, and a text-shadow
   is composited ABOVE that clipped background -- it would darken the letters
   themselves instead of the field around them. drop-shadow works off the
   element's rendered alpha, so it comes out glyph-shaped and leaves no box. */
---
<div data-bar="" style="position:absolute;left:48px;right:48px;top:52vh;z-index:30;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;font-family:'SN Ja Mono',ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace;font-weight:300;font-size:22.5px;letter-spacing:.22em;transition:top 900ms cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1);--cap-sep:drop-shadow(0 0 .5em rgba(0,0,0,.95)) drop-shadow(0 0 1.6em rgba(0,0,0,.9)) drop-shadow(0 0 3.4em rgba(0,0,0,.8))">
<div data-bar-track="" style="display:contents">
<button type="button" data-slot="" data-i="0" style="font:inherit;letter-spacing:inherit;border:0;background:none;padding:0;color:rgba(217,225,234,0.45);cursor:pointer;transition:color 300ms ease;white-space:nowrap;opacity:0;filter:var(--cap-sep)">REAL-TIME CONTENT</button>
<button type="button" data-slot="" data-i="1" style="font:inherit;letter-spacing:inherit;border:0;background:none;padding:0;color:rgba(217,225,234,0.45);cursor:pointer;transition:color 300ms ease;white-space:nowrap;opacity:0;filter:var(--cap-sep)">SCREENS PRODUCTION</button>
<button type="button" data-slot="" data-i="2" style="font:inherit;letter-spacing:inherit;border:0;background:none;padding:0;color:rgba(217,225,234,0.45);cursor:pointer;transition:color 300ms ease;white-space:nowrap;opacity:0;filter:var(--cap-sep)">MIXED REALITY</button>
<button type="button" data-slot="" data-i="3" style="font:inherit;letter-spacing:inherit;border:0;background:none;padding:0;color:rgba(217,225,234,0.45);cursor:pointer;transition:color 300ms ease;white-space:nowrap;opacity:0;filter:var(--cap-sep)">EQUIPMENT RENTAL</button>
</div>
{/* Mobile-only single-line marquee of the active section's subs. Populated + shown by the
    controller (data-mq on [data-bar]); display:none everywhere by default. */}
<div data-sub-marquee="" aria-hidden="true" style="display:none"><div data-sub-track=""></div></div>
</div>
